                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A short puzzle game released roughly ten years ago that's about escapism; more specifically, a woman deciding to leave her unsatisfying office job to become a shepherd, along the way crossing paths with coworkers either wishing her the best or chiding her for giving up all she's accomplished so far, either way turning into the flock of sheep that she protects. The addition of Steam Trading Cards will elongate your play time if you care about those, but if you don't, a single playthrough from start to end can be just a quarter of an hour due to how simple the puzzles are, and a base price of $2.59 CAD feels a tad much for so little. It's style is absolutely lovely to look at, though, and that solitary point is just enough to tip my decision into a recommendation.",
